WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:05.430
Narrator: The first teaser for the final

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:07.982
season of Game of Thrones debuted on HBO.

00:00:07.982 --> 00:00:09.870
[Crowd Yells]

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:11.490
So far, the only footage we've seen from

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.110
the season was in a trailer for

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.370
HBO's 2019 lineup.

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:17.670
There, we saw Daenerys Targaryen

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:20.550
and Sansa Stark meeting
for the very first time.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:22.960
Rather than giving us
a clip of new footage

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:24.780
we instead got an extended scene that will

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.700
not actually end up in the final season.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.760
Naturally, it left us with a lot more

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:31.860
questions than answers.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.253
The teaser is called "The
Crypts of Winterfell."

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:41.890
The first thing we see
is Jon Snow walking down

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:44.240
a dark hallway in Winterfell's crypts with

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:45.500
torch in hand.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.150
He walks past a statue of Lyanna Stark.

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:49.110
That's when we hear:

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.230
Lyanna: You have to protect him.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:52.990
Narrator: This is a
call back to season six

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:55.460
episode 10, "The Winds of Winter."

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:57.990
It's in the Tower of Joy, which we see

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:00.730
in a flashback of sorts
thanks to Bran Stark

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:03.200
who is now the Three-Eyed Raven.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.890
In the scene, Lyanna has just given birth

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:09.356
to Jon, and Ned arrives
at the guarded fortress.

00:01:09.356 --> 00:01:11.381
Lyanna: Ned?

00:01:11.381 --> 00:01:12.620
Ned: Lyanna?

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:13.993
Lyanna: If Robert finds out he'll

00:01:13.993 --> 00:01:16.410
kill him. You know he will.

00:01:17.366 --> 00:01:19.920
You have to protect him.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.010
Narrator: Lyanna is asking Ned

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:23.770
to protect Jon from Robert Baratheon.

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:27.260
Robert, at that time, was
supposed to marry Lyanna

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:29.350
but Jon isn't Robert's child.

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:31.923
No, he's Rhaegar Targaryen's son.

00:01:33.069 --> 00:01:35.260
Lyanna and Rhaegar's affair, of course

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:38.780
made Robert mad, leading
to Robert's rebellion

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:41.670
which ended with Robert
on the Iron Throne.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.710
But more than anything, this scene

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:46.750
is definitive proof that
Jon is a Stark by blood

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.040
and also has a claim to
the throne because he's

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:51.380
Rhaegar Targaryen's son, which makes

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:54.750
John a Targaryen, descendant
of Aerys Targaryen

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:56.380
the Mad King.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:57.523
Aerys:Burn them all.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.280
Narrator: Obviously at this point,

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:02.190
Jon doesn't know he has Targaryen blood

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:05.752
because he wouldn't have, you know.

00:02:05.752 --> 00:02:09.126
Lyanna: You have to protect him.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:13.420
Narrator: Now the next one

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:15.290
might seem like a minor detail

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:17.550
but it's actually very important.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:19.270
In the teaser, we see a feather

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:20.670
land on the ground.

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:22.030
Later in the teaser we'll see

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:24.470
that same feather freeze.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:26.100
The feather is actually a callback

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.800
all the way to the pilot

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:29.940
when then-King Robert Baratheon places

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.270
it on Lyanna's crypt statue.

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:33.840
We saw it again in the fourth episode of

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.610
season five, "Sons of the
Harpy," in which Sansa

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:39.280
visiting her aunt's statue

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:40.723
sees it and picks it up.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.270
The truth about Jon Snow is hinted

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:47.290
at in both episodes featuring the feather.

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:49.720
In the pilot, King Robert and Ned discuss

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:52.290
Rhaegar and Lyanna for the first time.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:53.730
When Robert says he dreams of

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.720
killing Rhaegar every night

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:58.840
Ned replies by saying,
"The Targaryens are gone."

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:01.940
"Not all of them," Robert replies.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:03.898
The episode then cuts to Daenerys

00:03:03.898 --> 00:03:05.800
and Viserys Targaryen

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.380
but we now know that they weren't

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:09.363
the last surviving Targaryens.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:13.110
The feather's second
appearance is in season five

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:14.960
when Sansa visits the crypts after

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:16.850
returning to Winterfell.

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:18.800
While standing at Lyanna's crypt

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.813
she notices the feather and picks it up.

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:25.470
She and Littlefinger discuss

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:27.970
what happened between Rhaegar and Lyanna.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:30.010
Sansa repeats a widely accepted

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:31.680
falsehood about Rhaegar and Lyanna.

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.290
Sansa: He kidnapped her and raped her.

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:35.123
Narrator: That he captured her

00:03:35.123 --> 00:03:36.950
against her will, and brought her

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.690
to the Tower of Joy, but
Rhaegar and Lyanna were

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:43.650
actually in love and
secretly eloped together.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:45.450
Rhaegar: I am her's
Lyanna: I am his

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:47.240
Rhaegar: and she is mine
Lyanna: and he is mine

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:49.133
Both: from this day

00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:51.173
Both: until the end of my days.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:53.120
Bran: Robert's rebellion was

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:53.993
built on a lie.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:57.000
Narrator: Littlefinger
doesn't correct Sansa

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.167
but instead gives her a knowing smirk.

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:06.710
Catelyn: All this horror
has come to my family.

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:07.890
Narrator: Next in the teaser

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:09.620
we cut to see Sansa walking down

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:11.310
that same passageway.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:13.560
She walks past the Catelyn statue

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.760
which seems to almost whisper to her.

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:19.110
Catelyn: All this horror
has come to my family.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.350
Narrator: We then see Arya Stark.

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:24.880
In the background, we hear
the rest of this quote.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:26.070
Catelyn: It's only because I couldn't

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:27.323
love a motherless child.

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:29.770
Narrator: The full quote is:

00:04:30.618 --> 00:04:31.750
Catelyn: All this horror has

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:33.017
come to my family.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:37.710
It's all because I couldn't

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.540
love a motherless child.

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:41.950
Narrator: This comes from season three

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:45.160
episode two, "Dark Wings, Dark Words."

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:48.090
She's talking to Talisa, Robb Stark's love

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:49.300
in the woods on the way to

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.450
Lord [Hoster] Tully's funeral.

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:53.220
Catelyn is under the impression that Jon

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:56.120
is Ned's illegitimate
child from an affair.

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:58.190
In this quote, she regrets not

00:04:58.190 --> 00:04:59.700
being a real mother to Jon and

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:01.620
letting jealousy take over.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:02.520
Catelyn: When my husband brought

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:03.800
that baby home from the war

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:06.370
I couldn't bear to look at him.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:07.650
Narrator: Catelyn died never knowing

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:09.330
the truth about Jon

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:11.250
but she's right about how Jon's entrance

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:14.010
into her family has complicated things.

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:16.420
But it could also be the thing that

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:17.630
sets things right

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:20.750
if Jon takes the throne at King's Landing.

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:23.040
Then, the teaser gives us a cameo from

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:24.360
another character that we haven't

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.020
heard from in ages.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:29.040
It's a statue of Ned Stark
whose season one death

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:31.560
in the episode "Baylor" shocked the world

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:33.853
and set the tone for the entire series.

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:37.410
Jon turns to the statue as we hear

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:38.660
Ned: You are a Stark.

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:42.200
You might not have my name, but you

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:43.320
have my blood.

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:44.480
Narrator: This was from season one

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:46.670
episode two, "Kingsroad."

00:05:46.670 --> 00:05:48.370
It's an important line.

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:50.350
Ned: You are a Stark.

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.190
You might not have my name, but you

00:05:53.029 --> 00:05:54.610
have my blood.

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:56.080
Narrator: This was perhaps our first hint

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:58.290
in the show at Jon's true parentage.

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:00.780
Back in season one, a lot of us thought

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:03.720
this was confirmation
that Jon was Ned's son

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:04.960
but turns out it's a bit more

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:06.890
complicated than that.

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:08.670
Ned said this as he sent Jon off

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:10.490
to become part of the Night's Watch

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:11.700
prompting Jon to ask if his

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:13.340
mother is still alive.

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:15.580
Then, Ned promises that the next time

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:16.470
they see each other

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:18.100
they'll talk about his mother.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:20.767
They never see each other again.

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:29.120
Finally, Jon, Sansa, and Arya unite.

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:32.290
The three of them look
upon statues of themselves

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:35.000
as if they'll be next
among Winterfell's dead.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.380
So we know the three siblings will

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:38.210
probably unite at Winterfell

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:40.160
and based on the earlier snippet

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:42.230
Daenarys will be there as well.

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:44.250
Sansa: Winterfell is yours, Your Grace.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:46.010
Narrator: Next, they draw their swords

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:48.293
and face off against the coming ice storm.

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:53.620
This feels like fairly
obvious foreshadowing

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:56.240
to the show's final epic battle.

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:57.520
The stage for this was set in the

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:00.600
season seven finale, "The
Dragon and the Wolf."

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:03.470
In the episode before this
one, "Beyond the Wall,"

00:07:03.470 --> 00:07:05.390
the wights and White Walkers successfully

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:07.503
killed Daenerys' dragon Viserion.

00:07:15.739 --> 00:07:17.690
The Night King then reanimates the dragon

00:07:17.690 --> 00:07:20.040
finally giving them a
weapon powerful enough

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:21.390
to bust through the wall and

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:23.073
make their way into Westeros.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:29.890
This teaser was just a taste

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:31.980
of what season eight will be like.

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:33.230
And while it didn't even show us

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:35.420
any actual footage from the new season

00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:38.110
it seems to perfectly set the tone.

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:40.370
But this was the most important

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:41.340
piece of information

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:43.850
from the teaser, the
eighth and final season

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:47.310
of Game of Thrones premieres
on Sunday, April 14.

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:49.260
Until then, we'll just have to wait

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:51.430
for the first trailer to debut.

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:54.330
So what did you think of the first teaser?

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:56.860
Does it give you any hints
about what's to come?

00:07:56.860 --> 00:07:58.423
Let us know in the comments.

